{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise","id":1491719,"title":"How Garou can go beyond her power-level (plot-wise)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-29T00:37:49-07:00","id":1491719,"title":"How Garou can go beyond her power-level (plot-wise)","content":"So, there is a huge gap between game mechanic and lore there. E.g., technicaly King Albrecht has a pretty discent chance to kill Mithra. But lore does not support it, since there were no duel where Garou killed Mathuselah. So, which explanation is needed? Support of some powerfull spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T01:44:12-07:00","id":1491723,"title":"","content":"Well yes, the help of spirits are quite possible for a legendary garou. You can bet he has a lot of rites and gifts extremely powerful, after all the rank 6 silver fang gift allow to instant kill any living dead, a rank 5 silent strider gift allow to simply deactivate any blood power may be it discipline healing (vampire will littrerally only have their stats to fight). And last but the most important, some gift allow to find any target you want, use it during the day and the vampire will be asleep. And even if he awake he will be unable to roll more dice than his humanity level wich is generally pretty low for ancient vampire (around 4/5 dot)<br /> <br /> Finally a garou rarely fight alone, if the ennemy is powerfull and smart even the most powerful garou will face him with good equipement, fetish or not and with support<br /> <br /> And it seems you do not know but the Antediluvian of the Setite clan has been killed by a garou of the silent strider. Before dying he cursed the tribe to be unable to come in their homeland, that's why silent strider are nomad.<br /> <br /> Vampire of the first generation are the most powerfull being of the world of darkness, but werewolves are the most dangerous of the world of darkness because thanks to spirits they theorically can get any power you can imagine as long as they find a spirit to teach them (including full immunity to any mental control like domination), and as living protector of earth and nature they can developp the faculty to call an army of spirits to fight with them.<br /> There's a lot of gift in the book that would allow them to resist the antediluvian, so if they have only 5 or 6 good gift they would simply destroy them<br /> <br /> Don't underastimate garou that would be a major mistake, if you read the Book of Nod and look for Cain's laws you'll see that even him, the first vampire, immortal, invincible, godly powered... Fear them and tell his infant to avoid them at any cost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 08-29-2022, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T01:53:01-07:00","id":1491724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491723#post1491723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally a garou rarely fight alone, if the ennemy is powerfull and smart even the most powerful garou will face him with good equipement, fetish or not and with support<br /> <br /> And it seems you do not know but the Antediluvian of the Setite clan has been killed by a garou of the silent strider. Before dying he cursed the tribe to be unable to come in their homeland, that's why silent strider are nomad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't underastimate garou that would be a major mistake x)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all game mechanic and not lore. IIRC it's not clear, was Seth killed by Shu Horus. Anyway, Yaga and Mithra usually mop the floor with Garou.<br /> As for Earth-protectors - they lost it, actually. Accordind to fifth edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 08-29-2022, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T02:30:48-07:00","id":1491726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise#post1491719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there is a huge gap between game mechanic and lore there. E.g., technicaly King Albrecht has a pretty discent chance to kill Mithra. But lore does not support it, since there were no duel where Garou killed Mathuselah. So, which explanation is needed? Support of some powerfull spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's vampire lore. Vampire lore doesn't really care about Werewolf lore or maths. Werewolves have killed worse than Methusahlehs. It was most likely Tuesday.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T02:38:13-07:00","id":1491727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491726#post1491726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's vampire lore. Vampire lore doesn't really care about Werewolf lore or maths. Werewolves have killed worse than Methusahlehs. It was most likely Tuesday.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtA has no actuall killed Mathusahlehs either. And wasn't Yaga and Mithra mentioned in Werewolf lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T02:54:59-07:00","id":1491728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491727#post1491727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA has no actuall killed Mathusahlehs either. And wasn't Yaga and Mithra mentioned in Werewolf lore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mithras doesn't appear in Werewolf. Yaga does, but she is placed as a Big Bad the Garou of Russia need to take down, along with her generals and the Zmei (giant dragons)... and then comes in Vampire and has her killed offscreen by a random new group of super Nosferatu.Yaga was supposed to be an epic undertaking for Werewolf, but was just treated as an offscreen slideshow murder in Vampire and never used again. Honestly, she never should have been a Vampire in the first place, as she would have been much more interesting as an ancient witch.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, a Werewolf and a kinfolk Mage apprentice of Isis managed to fight Set to a standstill. The fight ended with him killing/turning Nephtys, and Set having to curse the Silent Striders whose hero Shu-Horus was fighting him to never stand again in Egypt. He wasn't even able to kill Shu-Horus.<br /> <br /> It pays to remember that the games treat these things differently and that the whole &quot;kills packs of Garou to look cool&quot; is a narrative device to establish why someone is scary, not a substantive analysys of what the other game actually does and is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-29-2022, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T03:17:01-07:00","id":1491729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491728#post1491728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off the top of my head, a Werewolf and a kinfolk Mage apprentice of Isis managed to fight Set to a standstill. The fight ended with him killing/turning Nephtys, and Set having to curse the Silent Striders whose hero Shu-Horus was fighting him to never stand again in Egypt. He wasn't even able to kill Shu-Horus.<br /> <br /> It pays to remember that the games treat these things differently and that the whole &amp;quot;kills packs of Garou to look cool&amp;quot; is a narrative device to establish why someone is scary, not a substantive analysys of what the other game actually does and is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Still pretty vaguie. A whole bunch of variose supes couldn't take a one Atidevulian (AFAIK he was supported by Wyrm directly, tough) and Striders were cursed. It's not a true victory.<br /> <br /> 2) Kill Methusehlah is cool, too. But WW never ever let even the most renown Garou to do this.<br /> Hence, vampire-fans easily can mock WtA with 'you guys are shit only until the Elders show themselves'))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T03:27:52-07:00","id":1491730,"title":"","content":"It's White Wolf. Everything is vague.<br /> <br /> And who cares about what a subgroup of Vampire people think? If they really have to make themselves feel better about their game by pissing on other games, I feel sorry for them.<br /> I hope most of them have better things to do.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I'll enjoy Werewolf for what it is - a game of flawed heroes, family, sacrifice, spirituality and killing big bad monsters - including old vampires if they happen to be relevant to the game you're playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T03:38:02-07:00","id":1491732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491730#post1491730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile, I'll enjoy Werewolf for what it is - a game of flawed heroes, family, sacrifice, spirituality and killing big bad monsters - including old vampires if they happen to be relevant to the game you're playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit... deeper.<br /> Anyway, now we already know that all this sacriface, family and other quite stuff was all for nothing. Wyrm won anyway. And Garou didn't get even some glorious death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T03:51:46-07:00","id":1491734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491728#post1491728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head, a Werewolf and a kinfolk Mage apprentice of Isis managed to fight Set to a standstill. The fight ended with him killing/turning Nephtys, and Set having to curse the Silent Striders whose hero Shu-Horus was fighting him to never stand again in Egypt. He wasn't even able to kill Shu-Horus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The events revolving around Set and the other splats are some of the worst in terms of cross-over compatibility of lore, even outside of point-of-view biased narratives. It's a pretty good example for how you need some serious hand-waving if you want to mash up lore of the different lines.<br /> <br /> By the by, in WtA lore Shu-Horus killed Nephthys, who was a childe of Set at this point (and thus a 4th generation Methusehlah). I'm pretty sure I recall other instances, but can't name them on top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:19:37-07:00","id":1491740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491732#post1491732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a bit... deeper.<br /> Anyway, now we already know that all this sacriface, family and other quite stuff was all for nothing. Wyrm won anyway. And Garou didn't get even some glorious death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will they take your books and imagination away?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491734#post1491734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The events revolving around Set and the other splats are some of the worst in terms of cross-over compatibility of lore, even outside of point-of-view biased narratives. It's a pretty good example for how you need some serious hand-waving if you want to mash up lore of the different lines.<br /> <br /> By the by, in WtA lore Shu-Horus killed Nephthys, who was a childe of Set at this point (and thus a 4th generation Methusehlah). I'm pretty sure I recall other instances, but can't name them on top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I say kill, that's when he turned her into a vampire and his childer. He even takes her heart so she can never countermand him again. That was before the great Exodus of the Striders (Ancient Egypt). There's a whole storyline about trying to find her and give her final peace in Rage Accross Egypt (modern day).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T15:22:56-07:00","id":1491821,"title":"","content":"Since ordinary vampires can kill methusalehs, it's pretty easy to see how Garou can kill methusalehs. Single Garou tend to be more powerful than single vampires; they can operate during the day; and they usually operate as a group.<br /> <br /> That the game does not have lore showing this is simply because it was not needed for the purposes of the game books. Including a story about how a single Garou or pack killed some ancient vampire in the past has no relevance to a game book talking about today's events. It is just historical trivia. Now the Garou likely have lots of legends about werewolves killing some ancient vampire. They also have lots of legends about defeating all sorts of Wyrm creatures. But we're not told those except in a few cases where the legend in question has importance to the chronicle setting. If you are interested in that, you have to create your own legends.<br /> <br /> We hear about Mithras, Baba Yaga, and the All High because they are currently active and thus part of the active setting. We don't hear about some ancient vampire called Grendel, because the Garou Beowulf destroyed him and his Dam fifteen hundred years ago, and that is now irrelevant to the needs of the game books. That would only come up in some tribal or sept specific lore, or because of contact with Ancestors.<br /> <br /> But since Vampire has lots of lore about vampires being terrified of the Lupines, it's a good bet. And we know that in Los Angeles By Night, that the Anarchs didn't kill Don Sebastian and his court of elders. The book makes it quite clear the Anarchs would have lost. Instead, the Anarchs arrived after a Lupine attack killed the Prince and the other elders. They weren't methusalehs, but that was still pretty potent. Combined with the canonical events of Under a Blood Red Moon, there is lots of lore that Garou can be devastating to vampires. We know this because these specific examples were important to understanding the current setting.<br /> <br /> Now, I will say that the stupidest thing you can do is try to fight a vampire at night. Anyone smart will prefer to hunt them during the day when they are at their weakest. So unless there is an immediate reason why you must fight at night (such as them attacking you), a lot of Garou lore is probably about them finding the clues on where they are hiding during the day, and destroying them then. With lots of emphasis on the moment it wakes from slumber and briefly struggles right before the Garou destroy the creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:26:41-07:00","id":1491848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491723#post1491723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it seems you do not know but the Antediluvian of the Setite clan has been killed by a garou of the silent strider. Before dying he cursed the tribe to be unable to come in their homeland, that's why silent strider are nomad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was that stated? The war between the Setites and the Silent Striders took place around 1800 BC. And Set was known to be active long after that. For example he personally fought in the Baali Wars in 1500 BC. He didn't officially vanish until 33 AD, almost 1900 years after cursing the Silent Striders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:30:10-07:00","id":1491856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491734#post1491734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the by, in WtA lore Shu-Horus killed Nephthys, who was a childe of Set at this point (and thus a 4th generation Methusehlah).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a little (but relevant) correction, she was not a Methuselah.<br /> <br /> While Generation gives a lot of power, age is still a big theme of the game, and Methuselah specifically refers either to a vampire above 1 thousand years old, or one that underwent a strange psychological transformation that takes place at some moment after at least 1 thousand years of life.<br /> <br /> Many players and STs like to make a stricter link between Gen and being called Methuselah, but that's not LaW (Lore as Written).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T01:10:16-07:00","id":1491877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491848#post1491848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where was that stated? The war between the Setites and the Silent Striders took place around 1800 BC. And Set was known to be active long after that. For example he personally fought in the Baali Wars in 1500 BC. He didn't officially vanish until 33 AD, almost 1900 years after cursing the Silent Striders.</div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't killed, but he was defeated. It looked like Sutekh was losing, that's when he resorted to taking out and turning Nephtys (a sorceror that may or may not have been using vampire blood to fuel her spells). Still Shu-Horus fought Sutekh to s standstill, and bought the time for the other Striders to spring a trap that &quot;imprisoned him in the Earth&quot;. But the last thing Sutekh did was to curse the line of the Striders, forever causing them pain and suffering while they stood in their homelands.<br /> <br /> (Silent Striders Revised pp. 18 - The Great Diaspora)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-30T10:15:05-07:00","id":1491919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491724#post1491724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all game mechanic and not lore. IIRC it's not clear, was Seth killed by Shu Horus. Anyway, Yaga and Mithra usually mop the floor with Garou.<br /> As for Earth-protectors - they lost it, actually. Accordind to fifth edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly certain that I can trick out some Garou mechanically well enough to kill both of them at the same time (stat boosting Gifts are a hell of a drug... delivered by a damage-doubling fang dagger). And, if need be, there's always the nuclear option of &quot;Mokole literally the size of Godzilla right out of chargen&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-08T05:51:11-07:00","id":1494593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1491719-how-garou-can-go-beyond-her-power-level-plot-wise?p=1491919#post1491919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fairly certain that I can trick out some Garou mechanically well enough to kill both of them at the same time (stat boosting Gifts are a hell of a drug... delivered by a damage-doubling fang dagger). And, if need be, there's always the nuclear option of &quot;Mokole literally the size of Godzilla right out of chargen&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you optimize the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1436799-w20-enhancing-the-pack-optimal-initial-char-gen-pack\">Pack</a>, you can kill Methuselahs with starting characters. If you want an individual breakdown on how to do this, see my build <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1302751-low-generation-vampires-vs-werewolves-v20?p=1302784#post1302784\">Ugly McAngry</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-08-2022, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}